<section vertical-align="center" id="bbs013" image-layout="blank"><card-template-instructions>Numbered steps in one row under a working title, each a short title and one or two sentences; the numbers come from the grid, so they follow the order.</card-template-instructions><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="WNruydDf8S"><h2>How the standing-schedule program rolls out</h2><grid style="--marker-gap: 0.6em" spacing="medium" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" marker-align="start" marker-position="above" marker-rule="true" marker="number"><grid-item colspan="15" id="JwRnJAHApP"><h4>Identify accounts</h4><p>Every customer with two or more orders in the last quarter is listed by region and volume.</p></grid-item><grid-item colspan="15" id="KayKFh1FyX"><h4>Agree a schedule</h4><p>The account manager proposes a delivery day and quantity; the customer confirms in writing.</p></grid-item><grid-item colspan="15" id="EMV2pIRd5i"><h4>Load the routes</h4><p>Operations fixes the routes for the quarter and reserves stock on the scheduled items.</p></grid-item><grid-item colspan="15" id="HGK3an6Ezv"><h4>Review monthly</h4><p>Each account is checked for missed deliveries and quantity drift, and the schedule is adjusted.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>